{"agent":"impl-hx-facts","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`problems` is documented as validating the fact record `{v, s, src, d, ver?, note?}` where only `ver` and `note` are optional, but it never checks the required `v` field. For example, `problems(\"facts.example\", {\"s\": \"verified\", \"src\": \"tool\", \"d\": \"2024-01-01\"})` returns `[]`, so an incomplete fact with no value is treated as defect-free. Downstream code that assumes a fact has a value can then fail or treat the missing value as valid.","digest":"b50f897aa115b269","location":"ddflow/services/facts.py:problems","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/facts.py:problems"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`_present` uses truthiness to decide whether a descriptor field is present, so legitimate falsey values (`False`, `0`, `\"\"`, `[]`, `{}`) are silently omitted. For example, a section field `env = {}` is a descriptor value, but line 59 evaluates `(v := getattr(sec, sf.name))` as false and does not add `section.env` to the result. `rows` then produces no row for that fact, and `validate` (line 91) can reject an explicit overlay such as `[facts.\"section.env\"] s = \"verified\"` with “status verified needs a value” even though the descriptor does have the value.","digest":"ee03042837151e0e","location":"ddflow/services/harnessfacts.py:_present (line 59)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/harnessfacts.py:_present (line 59)"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"For reserved sections, `none = true` does not suppress the section’s values. If `h.reserved[\"x\"].none` is true but `h.reserved[\"x\"].values` is `{\"a\": \"1\"}`, `_present` emits both `x: (\"none\", True)` and `x.a: (\"1\", False)`. `rows` then shows a value under a section documented as absent, and `validate` will accept an overlay for `x.a` with a readable status because the value is present. This contradicts the documented “section says none = true reads as status none” behavior and differs from the normal-section path, which `continue`s after seeing `none`.","digest":"f03a4b16b8b800bb","location":"ddflow/services/harnessfacts.py:_present (lines 62-65)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/harnessfacts.py:_present (lines 62-65)"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`table` only replaces `|` in the `value` cell. Other interpolated fields, especially `source` from an overlay `src`, are not sanitized. Given an overlay entry with `src = \"a|b\"`, the generated markdown row contains an extra pipe and becomes an eight-column row under a seven-column header, corrupting the rendered facts table.","digest":"8338ec90277ef638","location":"ddflow/services/harnessfacts.py:table (line 126)","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/services/harnessfacts.py:table (line 126)"},{"chunk":6,"detail":"The `id=\"opencode\"` filter assertion does not verify that any rows are actually returned. It only checks `all(r[\"agent\"] == \"opencode\" for r in out.data[\"facts\"])`, and `all()` is true for an empty iterable. If `harness_view` returns `exit=0`, a message containing `\"opencode\"`, but an empty `facts` list (for example because the filter compares the wrong field or accidentally drops all rows), this test still passes. Thus the id filter can be broken and the test will not catch it.","digest":"0b60692e8ba11ff2","location":"tests/test_harness_facts.py:test_view_facts_table_filters","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_harness_facts.py:test_view_facts_table_filters"}],"chunks_total":6,"coverage":"6/6 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":23137,"diff_sha":"ad6f4b8de914ef1f5560fbb096e6e3fb8c135f494b52fd1a28a18831c4c71826","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":581.9,"excluded_bytes":1943,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_cli_help.ambr"],"family":"alibaba","findings":5,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","output_digest":"f6035b10d98e512c","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/HX-facts-core.rubber_duck.qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8.20261030T071843Z-f1c11237.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4,5,6],"reviewed_head":"9e9fc46a3b054292013d09adc8f974bfbaffe047","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/harness.py":"100644 a3361832d46a89f54ec1d2c78c02809dc1efa8ec","ddflow/services/context_families.py":"100644 03ee5134b9412fddcd5d07825592ae07e80b69c5","ddflow/services/facts.py":"100644 f16e5d5f6ad72a09e5849432dba96e9ad3c13f96","ddflow/services/harnessfacts.py":"100644 1bc7890a7d1314ff52fb4b091290b1e373eb27de","ddflow/services/harnessreg.py":"100644 1ea23c5a31460c2515bbdff74cb8b223afae466c","ddflow/surfaces/commands/harness.py":"100644 12db8058d1491a0abdc6cb7ecdac1747683f1219","ddflow/surfaces/declared/hooks.py":"100644 65da60f70e9c6ead5007b6878e06a6411361d053","ddflow/surfaces/parsers/workflow.py":"100644 b5a91fa370920b9c6711da0c092937bad8a66b6d","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_cli_help.ambr":"100644 4d7c8936702f483bc758df1fecbcf1d3f5195834","tests/test_harness_facts.py":"100644 cbc68c010e0e619939c9d9076af0ff876f51e213"},"reviewer":"qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/facts.py:problems","ddflow/services/harnessfacts.py:_present (line 59)","ddflow/services/harnessfacts.py:_present (lines 62-65)","ddflow/services/harnessfacts.py:table (line 126)","tests/test_harness_facts.py:test_view_facts_table_filters"],"tree_sha":"1cae32dea5f0+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":2},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"5 finding(s)"},"id":"ef8a82218f17ad794c766784f","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":113861,"schema":1,"subject":"HX-facts-core","ts":"2026-10-30T07:37:06.935010Z"}
